    {
      "id": 17,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Develop a portable single-threaded baseline that combines sparse row-wise blockers with an in-place DP scan; investigate fast input and ARM64-friendly prefix-scan/vectorization while preserving duplicate/start/destination blocker correctness.\",\"B\":\"Investigate a correctness-safe hybrid algorithm: dense in-place row DP for small/moderate n and combinatorial obstacle DP for sparse, very large grids. Define an input-dependent crossover without specializing to benchmark values.\",\"C\":\"Refine the measured best OpenMP segmented prefix-scan approach for 4 ARM64 cores: remove avoidable synchronization/work, verify carry propagation at segment blockers and n=1, and compare compact blocker layouts against the dense bitmap.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only measured improvements, starting from C's 0.02288s candidate. Test combinations of OpenMP segmented DP and sparse/row-oriented blocking; retain the fastest correct whole program rather than assuming component gains add.\",\"analysis\":\"The baseline performs quadratic dense-grid work plus a row copy. Measured wins show in-place DP is essential; C's 4-core segmented scan is currently best (0.02288s), narrowly ahead of B's sparse NEON implementation (0.02524s). Dense and sparse formulations have different asymptotic/memory tradeoffs under the stated broad constraints, so research should preserve correctness across both rather than tune to a single observed input. The quadratic obstacle predecessor proposal is slower than baseline and should not be integrated unchanged.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"93dda24d1ab3ad6a2b53bcec3af9baa68f174d7f90ba13e413207974cf67a05e\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Develop a portable single-threaded baseline that combines sparse row-wise blockers with an in-place DP scan; investigate fast input and ARM64-friendly prefix-scan/vectorization while preserving duplicate/start/destination blocker correctness.\",\"B\":\"Investigate a correctness-safe hybrid algorithm: dense in-place row DP for small/moderate n and combinatorial obstacle DP for sparse, very large grids. Define an input-dependent crossover without specializing to benchmark values.\",\"C\":\"Refine the measured best OpenMP segmented prefix-scan approach for 4 ARM64 cores: remove avoidable synchronization/work, verify carry propagation at segment blockers and n=1, and compare compact blocker layouts against the dense bitmap.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only measured improvements, starting from C's 0.02288s candidate. Test combinations of OpenMP segmented DP and sparse/row-oriented blocking; retain the fastest correct whole program rather than assuming component gains add.\",\"analysis\":\"The baseline performs quadratic dense-grid work plus a row copy. Measured wins show in-place DP is essential; C's 4-core segmented scan is currently best (0.02288s), narrowly ahead of B's sparse NEON implementation (0.02524s). Dense and sparse formulations have different asymptotic/memory tradeoffs under the stated broad constraints, so research should preserve correctness across both rather than tune to a single observed input. The quadratic obstacle predecessor proposal is slower than baseline and should not be integrated unchanged.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"nonce\":\"2d4021c64f2e435791325becbddd1a72\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"medium\",\"request_sha256\":\"93dda24d1ab3ad6a2b53bcec3af9baa68f174d7f90ba13e413207974cf67a05e\",\"session_id\":\"6c21751f3d074f408f5a1ddbc2a924a7\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"7d89bc6b3865f97e7054081728dacdecdcc0718b142e2b52e5341196f7c4330a\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":17249,\"output_tokens\":534,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":230}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-5.6-terra\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"medium\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":17783,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
      "created": 1792118983.6025283
